-- ===========================================================================
-- Warlock: Backlash redesign -- Soulstone cheats death
-- ===========================================================================
--
-- TODO.md: "Damage that would otherwise kill you instead consumes your
--           Soulstone and heals you for 20% of your maximum health."
--
-- Ranks: 34935 / 34938 / 34939 (talent 1817, Destruction).
--
-- Effect1 changes from SPELL_AURA_PROC_TRIGGER_SPELL (42) to
-- SPELL_AURA_SCHOOL_ABSORB (69) with EffectMiscValue1 = 127 (all schools).
-- The absorb is what gives spell_warl_backlash_cheat_death
-- (src/WarlockBacklash.cpp) a hook on incoming damage; the script sets the
-- pool to unlimited and then soaks only damage that would be lethal.
-- EffectSpellClassMaskA1 is zeroed -- it held the old Shadow Bolt/Incinerate
-- mask, which is meaningless (and misleading) on an absorb effect.
--
-- Effect2 (SPELL_AURA_MOD_SPELL_CRIT_CHANCE, +1/2/3%) is deliberately KEPT --
-- it is the sensible half of the original talent.
--
-- ProcFlags/ProcChance are cleared because the talent no longer procs;
-- DurationIndex 21 (permanent) is left as-is since this is a passive.
--
-- Spell 200400 is the heal itself, cloned from Guardian Spirit's heal
-- (48153) which is already a plain self-targeted SPELL_EFFECT_HEAL.
-- Its amount is always passed in as a custom basepoint by the script
-- (20% of max health), so the DBC value is irrelevant.
-- ===========================================================================



